      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "The polar piperidine alcohol [18F]FEP-4MOH, a small ionizable amine without lipophilic substituents, showed very low brain uptake (<0.05% dose/g) after IV dosing; this is the closest polar-amine phenotype and supports poor CNS access for the dicationic guanidine-azocane query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
